---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy Policy — DevFest.cz 2026"
	description="Privacy policy for DevFest.cz 2026 — how we collect, use, and protect your personal data."
>
	<main class="policy">
		<div class="policy-inner">
			<a href="/" class="back-link">&#8592; Back</a>

			<h1 class="policy-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p class="policy-meta">GUG.cz, z.s. · Last updated: June 2026</p>

			<section>
				<h2>1. Who we are</h2>
				<p>
					DevFest.cz 2026 is organised by GUG.cz, z.s. (formerly GDG Czech Republic),
					a volunteer community group. For privacy-related enquiries, contact us at
					<a href="mailto:devfest@gug.cz">devfest@gug.cz</a>.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>2. Data we collect and why</h2>

				<h3>a) Newsletter sign-up</h3>
				<p>
					When you submit your email address via the notification form, we store it in
					SmartEmailing (our email service provider) to send you conference updates such as
					ticket availability announcements and event news. Legal basis: consent (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a)).
					You may unsubscribe at any time via the link in every email.
				</p>

				<h3>b) Analytics cookies</h3>
				<p>
					If you accept cookies, we use Google Firebase Analytics (measurement ID G-L5NK2S2EZ0)
					to collect anonymised usage statistics — pages visited, session duration, browser type —
					so we can improve the website. No personally identifiable information is included.
					Legal basis: consent (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a)). You can withdraw consent at any time by
					clicking "Decline" in the cookie banner (clear your browser storage to see it again).
				</p>

				<h3>c) Server logs</h3>
				<p>
					Our hosting provider (Firebase Hosting) automatically records standard access logs
					(IP address, browser, requested URL). These are retained for up to 30 days for
					security purposes. Legal basis: legitimate interests (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)).
				</p>

				<h3>d) Bot protection (reCAPTCHA)</h3>
				<p>
					To protect our ticketing data from automated scraping and abuse, the site uses
					Google reCAPTCHA Enterprise (via Firebase App Check). reCAPTCHA runs in the background to
					tell humans from bots, analysing signals such as your interactions with the page,
					device and browser information, and IP address. This data is shared with Google and
					processed under the
					<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a>
					and
					<a href="https://policies.google.com/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Terms of Service</a>.
					Because this is a security measure, it runs regardless of your cookie choice.
					Legal basis: legitimate interests (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)).
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>3. Cookies</h2>
				<p>We use the following cookies:</p>
				<table>
					<caption class="sr-only">List of cookies we set, their purpose, and retention period.</caption>
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th scope="col">Name</th>
							<th scope="col">Purpose</th>
							<th scope="col">Duration</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row"><code>cookie-consent</code></th>
							<td>Stores your cookie preference (localStorage)</td>
							<td>Until you clear browser storage</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row"><code>_ga, _ga_*</code></th>
							<td>Google Analytics — only set after consent</td>
							<td>2 years</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row"><code>_GRECAPTCHA</code></th>
							<td>Google reCAPTCHA — bot protection (set for security, not consent-gated)</td>
							<td>6 months</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>4. Data sharing</h2>
				<p>
					We do not sell your data. We share it only with the processors listed above
					(SmartEmailing, Google Firebase, Google reCAPTCHA) under data processing agreements,
					and only to the extent necessary to provide the services described.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>5. Your rights</h2>
				<p>Under GDPR you have the right to:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
					<li>Request correction or deletion of your data</li>
					<li>Withdraw consent at any time (this does not affect prior processing)</li>
					<li>Lodge a complaint with the Czech Data Protection Authority (<a href="https://www.uoou.cz" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">uoou.cz</a>)</li>
				</ul>
				<p>To exercise these rights, email us at <a href="mailto:devfest@gug.cz">devfest@gug.cz</a>.</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>6. Changes to this policy</h2>
				<p>
					We may update this policy as the website evolves. The "last updated" date at the top
					reflects the most recent revision. Material changes will be announced via our newsletter.
				</p>
			</section>
		</div>
	</main>
</BaseLayout>

<style lang="scss">
	@use './privacy-policy';
</style>
